---
/**
 * The opening claim.
 *
 * Both halves of the work are the same instinct: policy enforced on every
 * instruction, and AI output that does not ship until something checked it.
 * The statement names that instinct, then hands over something the visitor
 * can check without leaving the page.
 *
 * Written to be read by someone who does not know what an ELF section is.
 * The jargon that remains is named the first time it is used.
 */
import { person, dissertation } from "@/data/site";
import { papers } from "@/data/publications";

// Counted from the record rather than typed in, so the headline number cannot
// drift away from the list further down the page.
const settled = papers.filter((p) => p.status !== "under review").length;
const reviewing = papers.length - settled;
---

<section id="text" data-section=".text" class="scroll-mt-24">
  <p class="t-label text-muted">{person.line}</p>

  <h1 class="t-display mt-6 max-w-[22ch]">
    Nothing is trusted until it is checked.
  </h1>

  <p class="t-body measure mt-7 text-muted">
    I build tools that check their own output. My Ph.D. work takes a security
    rule written in plain C code and carries it all the way into the compiled
    program, so the processor enforces it on every single instruction. My other
    work puts AI agents to work writing firmware and refuses to merge a line of
    it without evidence that it is correct.
  </p>

  <p class="t-body measure mt-5 text-muted">
    The diagram below is my dissertation, drawn from its own source code. The
    access-control rules it enforces are
    <a
      href="#policy_meta"
      class="text-ink underline decoration-rule-strong underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-allow"
      >running further down this page</a
    >, so you can try them yourself rather than take my word for it.
  </p>

  <!-- The three facts a reader needs before deciding to keep going. -->
  <dl
    class="mt-10 grid gap-px border-y border-rule-strong bg-rule sm:grid-cols-3"
  >
    <div class="bg-ground py-5 pr-6">
      <dt class="t-label text-muted">Dissertation</dt>
      <dd class="t-title mt-2 text-allow">{dissertation.degree}</dd>
      <dd class="t-small mt-1 text-muted">
        {dissertation.short} — expected {dissertation.expected}
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-ground py-5 pr-6 sm:pl-6">
      <dt class="t-label text-muted">Speed of the check</dt>
      <dd class="t-title mt-2">O(1), always</dd>
      <dd class="t-small mt-1 text-muted">
        The same cost whether there are ten rules or ten thousand
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-ground py-5 pr-6 sm:pl-6">
      <dt class="t-label text-muted">Papers</dt>
      <dd class="t-title mt-2">{settled} published or accepted</dd>
      <dd class="t-small mt-1 text-muted">
        Plus {reviewing} under review, across IEEE, ACM and MDPI
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
